From: Sutou Kouhei <kou@clear-code.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:03:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] GH-51690: [C++] Don't define __SSE2__ globally with MSVC
 (#53952)

### Rationale for this change

`simdjson >= 5` uses GCC builtins such as `__builtin_ctz` when `__SSE2__` is defined. So we can't build Apache Arrow C++ with `simdjson >= 5` and MSVC because we define `__SSE2__` globally.

### What changes are included in this PR?

We don't need to define `__SSE2__` because xsimd detects SSE2 by `_M_X64` with MSVC.

We still need to define `__SSE4_1__`/`__SSE4_2__` for xsimd because MSVC doesn't define them even with `/arch:SSE4.2`. But we define them only where SSE4.2 is enabled. So they are no longer defined with `ARROW_SIMD_LEVEL=NONE`.

### Are these changes tested?

Yes.

### Are there any user-facing changes?

Yes.

